This class taught me a lot. As someone who shutters whenever I hear the word "coding"
there were many times I did not feel fit for this class. I always assumed myself to 
just not be good at coding after past experiences where things never seemed to come
easily to me no matter how much studying or office hours I would attend. Early on
when working on the first project I felt inadequate and compared my very poor beginner 
level work to that of my classmates who seemed like they knew what they were doing. I
was not happy with my first project at all so from then on i changed the way I viewed creating
my work. I planned things out physically on paper (advice from TA Lilly) and began adding more 
notes on my own code even if it seemed obvious just so I could understand things better. I would
watch and follow tutorials on youtube and learn new things here and there to incorporate in my
own code. I started playing around more and learning about new little features i could add. Since then
I have been excited for the next project and to see what I can come up with and new extra little features 
i could add here and there. My latest project is probably my favorite and I am not only proud of myself
for growing with my skill but also for not comparing my work to others and just simply having fun creating.
I would give myself a B+/A- and I am very happy with that. I look forward to next quarter and hope
I can learn to better retain some things instead of sometimes going back to old projects to see how I did things. 
